{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"6bd9a704cb8bff28bdfad8180667defaf36e29d89b0a39cdacf41cf034920bce","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review sidecar result persistence","key_entities":["code_review_result_v1","code_review_result_v2","src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml","src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py","src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py","code_review_coach","code_review_decide","build_payload","latest_code_review_result","blocking","advisory","dropped","indeterminate","block_threshold","blocking_enabled","verification","decision","norm_id"],"problem_keywords":["sidecar","lossless persistence","code review findings","dropped findings","indeterminate findings","block threshold","schema migration","all buckets"],"propositions":["Code-review sidecar currently persists only surfaced findings (blocking, advisory, coaching) and omits dropped and indeterminate findings produced by Pass-3.","Code-review findings lack the resolved block_threshold and blocking_enabled values that Pass-3 determination produces, preventing full recovery of the complete finding list.","The code-review sidecar schema must be bumped from v1 to v2 to include all four buckets (blocking, advisory, dropped, indeterminate) with each finding retaining verification, decision, and threshold metadata.","The code_review_coach workflow step must accept and forward dropped and indeterminate buckets from the decide step into the terminal verdict dict.","The latest_code_review_result reader must accept both v1 and v2 schemas for backward compatibility, with v1 records remaining readable when new buckets are absent.","Surfaced-findings readers (novelty-floor consumer) must continue returning the blocking + advisory union unchanged from v2 payloads, preserving region-gating behavior."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785821371187896183,"uuid":"04ba0161-41a4-4087-ad32-2ba248537234"}